media: i2c: add an OmniVision OV48B2Q driver

The OV48B2Q is a 48 MP quad-Bayer sensor; on the Xiaomi Redmi Note 12 5G
(sunstone) it is the main camera, four CSI-2 lanes from a 24 MHz clock.
One mode: the binned 4000x3000 Bayer output at 30 fps, 1.8 Gbps per
lane, PDAF output off.

The register tables are those of MediaTek's ov48b2q_mipi_raw driver
(GPL-2.0, as shipped in LG's kernel sources), init and the 4000x3000
"preview" mode with the PDAF registers at the values its comments give
for "pd off"; exposure (0x3500, lines, even), gain (0x3508, 0x100 = 1x)
and frame length (0x380e) as that driver writes them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
index 5c52007f9..b8696fc63 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
@@ -558,6 +558,16 @@ config VIDEO_OV4689
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
 	  module will be called ov4689.
 
+config VIDEO_OV48B2Q
+	tristate "OmniVision OV48B2Q sensor support"
+	select V4L2_CCI_I2C
+	help
+	  This is a Video4Linux2 sensor driver for the OmniVision
+	  OV48B2Q camera.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
+	  module will be called ov48b2q.
+
 config VIDEO_OV5640
 	tristate "OmniVision OV5640 sensor support"
 	depends on OF
